 "post": {
  "title": "Why does your iPhone stop charging at 80%?",
  "caption": "Why does your iPhone stop charging at 80%? 🔋\n\nA lithium-ion battery wears faster the longer it sits fully charged. With Optimized Battery Charging, your iPhone learns your daily charging routine on the device, and when it expects a long charge it holds at 80% and aims to be full right when you unplug. On iPhone 15 and later you can also set a Charge Limit from 80% to 100%. Leave it on; if you need a full battery sooner, touch and hold the notification and tap Charge Now.\nSave this for the next time your phone stops at 80.",
